@GalLovesYT  I do know that she mentioned retinol which boosts your skin's cell turnover, sometimes making your skin feel thinner, even when it isn't, and retinol makes the skin sun sensitive, more than normal, which might mean that the skin could be more sensitive to the laser too?
I'd assume the AHA and BHA treatments before the laser were alright to use in the last hour before beginning laser treatment, because any affect that the acids would have on the skin wouldn't have any deep and substantial effects by the time the laser was used - it's probably a timing thing 🤷‍♀

Not a dermatologist, I thought it was strange too, this is just what I thought of to explain why the contradiction 🤣
